#: ../../source/docs/savetrim.rst:5
#: a3dfd2f101fe4a93b5a09d1104b9a72c
msgid "Save Steering Trim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/savetrim.rst:7
#: e7a2241d9079485f828868a4cc4cc49d
msgid "If the vehicle does not track straight in ``MANUAL`` mode with steering at neutral, you can either adjust the steering mechanics to correct, or use the ``RCx_OPTION`` =  5 (Save Trim) to correct. Using the steering channel's trim tab or sub-trim in the transmitter is not recommended (after RC calibration is completed), since it will appear as a constant pilot steering request in non-MANUAL modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/savetrim.rst:10
#: 3ba06e1c1863430198d8ccb31472be08
msgid "Save Trim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/savetrim.rst:12
#: 6381b50a05e74533a1714b8bbcc4625d
msgid "Activating Save Trim on the channel with RCx_OPTION = 5, will instantly capture the current output of the Steering Channel servo (normally SERVO1) and store it as its SERVOx_TRIM value. This can be repeated by de-activating and re-activating the rc channel function. The output is saved only at the moment of activation. It can be used in any mode except ``LOITER`` or ``HOLD``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/savetrim.rst:14
#: 1c7d5a06515349049f1f5079d696dc06
msgid "This is best used in ``ACRO`` mode when the autopilot is maintaining heading. Autonomous modes like ``AUTO`` or ``RTL``, may capture the output during a maneuver to turn to a waypoint, crosstrack correct, or be loitering at the end, and store incorrect results. But it can be used if careful as to when its applied. It can also be used during ``MANUAL`` mode by trimming at the transmitter for straight track, activating, and then returning the trim to center."
msgstr ""
